(1231860, 152807, 25397, '<td valign="top">Great photo there Bear, quality is superb. You know I just may have got who this was by if you included a boombox in the backround, but that would just ruin the whole picture so I''m glad you didn''t :-)<br/> <br/>And for those interested, "Ceci n''est pas une pipe" by Marcel Duchamp.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.tcf.ua.edu/Classes/Jbutler/T340/TreasonOfImagesShadow.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.tcf.ua.edu/Classes/Jbutler/T340/TreasonOfImagesShadowSmaller.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.tcf.ua.edu/Classes/Jbutler/T340/TreasonOfImagesShadowSmaller.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.tcf.ua.edu/Classes/Jbutler/T340/TreasonOfImagesShadowSmaller.jpg"/></a> <br/></td>', 'Great photo there Bear, quality is superb. You know I just may have got who this was by if you included a boombox in the backround, but that would just ruin the whole picture so I''m glad you didn''t :-) And for those interested, "Ceci n''est pas une pipe" by Marcel Duchamp.  ', '2005-03-16 10:51:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1231890, 152988, 26757, '<td valign="top">I Love it...<br/>Had I been able to log on last week, I would have given it a 9!  Really great.  I do find myself questioning the lighting balance though...  Wonder if it might have poped more with as a high-key photo, or a bit more contrast range... ie, a whiter white in the highlights and a deeper black in the shadow, more depth of shadow in the floor area, and wall behind.  Yes I know that you would have lost a bit more of the detail in the  blacks beneath the hand... but I still wonder if that loss might have been worth the PoP!<br/> <br/>Just my thoughts, and still I love it...  Wish I could have it for my twin son''s room... They''d get a kick out of a print like this!  <br/> <br/>Kudos!<br/>ginette</td>', 'I Love it...Had I been able to log on last week, I would have given it a 9!  Really great.  I do find myself questioning the lighting balance though...  Wonder if it might have poped more with as a high-key photo, or a bit more contrast range... ie, a whiter white in the highlights and a deeper black in the shadow, more depth of shadow in the floor area, and wall behind.  Yes I know that you would have lost a bit more of the detail in the  blacks beneath the hand... but I still wonder if that loss might have been worth the PoP! Just my thoughts, and still I love it...  Wish I could have it for my twin son''s room... They''d get a kick out of a print like this!   Kudos!ginette', '2005-03-16 10:57:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1231892, 154133, 4493, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by conceptphoto:</b></div><hr/><i>I hope the photo of the moon was at least yours. ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good point. I got a DQ a while back because I had a bug on a photo of the earth. Since I didn''t take the photo of the earth I was DQ''d. Wonder what the SC will do about this one.<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Originally posted by conceptphoto:I hope the photo of the moon was at least yours. ;-)   Good point. I got a DQ a while back because I had a bug on a photo of the earth. Since I didn''t take the photo of the earth I was DQ''d. Wonder what the SC will do about this one. -danny', '2005-03-16 10:58:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1231921, 154133, 28258, '<td valign="top">A truly inspiring display of creativity.  As I am fairly new to this site and photography, I am continually amazed at the talent pool here.  As I see your location of the picture taken, I am about 5 miles away in Fairfield.  Thank you for yet another great photograph.</td>', 'A truly inspiring display of creativity.  As I am fairly new to this site and photography, I am continually amazed at the talent pool here.  As I see your location of the picture taken, I am about 5 miles away in Fairfield.  Thank you for yet another great photograph.', '2005-03-16 11:04:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1231936, 154133, 19670, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue! I''m honored to have received a positive comment from the challenge winner. (BTW, I don''t see any reason the moon photo would have to be yours, as I read the rules. Existing art can be included in submissions as long as it''s not a literal representation of the work...so crabappl3''s DQ must have been for something else.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-16 11:16:14.</i></td>', 'Congratulations on your blue! I''m honored to have received a positive comment from the challenge winner. (BTW, I don''t see any reason the moon photo would have to be yours, as I read the rules. Existing art can be included in submissions as long as it''s not a literal representation of the work...so crabappl3''s DQ must have been for something else.)', '2005-03-16 11:11:31.000000', '2005-03-16 11:16:14.000000', 0),
(1231953, 153967, 34192, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone for your comments.  They are much appreciated.<br/>How I did this:  Chair - 2" tall, dead bush from backyard (trimmed to look more like a tree, spray painted black) magenta/red silk background (silk chosen for added texture, color chosen to stay away from yellow), black fleece blanket (chosen for complete lack of reflection), beads shaped like stars.<br/>I saturated the yellow and the red as far as possible without blowing out either color.<br/>I thought a ''textured'' background would work better - some agree and some disagree.  I am creating a better version of this shot with a little less texturing, more "star" looking stars and a lighter background.<br/>thanks again for all your input!<br/>dahkota<br/></td>', 'Thank you to everyone for your comments.  They are much appreciated.How I did this:  Chair - 2" tall, dead bush from backyard (trimmed to look more like a tree, spray painted black) magenta/red silk background (silk chosen for added texture, color chosen to stay away from yellow), black fleece blanket (chosen for complete lack of reflection), beads shaped like stars.I saturated the yellow and the red as far as possible without blowing out either color.I thought a ''textured'' background would work better - some agree and some disagree.  I am creating a better version of this shot with a little less texturing, more "star" looking stars and a lighter background.thanks again for all your input!dahkota', '2005-03-16 11:16:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1231954, 154154, 30214, '<td valign="top">my guess would be that it was a double exposure, but he had to paint the middle of the hand pitch black (with blurred edges) and  paint his face with a similar size eye-hole in it to avoid overlapping the images. Or (perhaps simpler) - he had two "complimentary" screens which he swapped before the second exposire. In any case - a magnificent job (I was sure it was going to get DQ''d :)). Congrats!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-16 11:19:13.</i></td>', 'my guess would be that it was a double exposure, but he had to paint the middle of the hand pitch black (with blurred edges) and  paint his face with a similar size eye-hole in it to avoid overlapping the images. Or (perhaps simpler) - he had two "complimentary" screens which he swapped before the second exposire. In any case - a magnificent job (I was sure it was going to get DQ''d :)). Congrats!', '2005-03-16 11:16:33.000000', '2005-03-16 11:19:13.000000', 0),
