(1233688, 154169, 34593, '<td valign="top">thank you everyone for your comments<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-17 00:46:40.</i></td>', 'thank you everyone for your comments', '2005-03-17 00:46:19.000000', '2005-03-17 00:46:40.000000', 0),
(1233816, 153371, 32511, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the votes and constructive candid feedback and of course the ribbon. What a confidence builder. As a newbe I am impressed with the welcome I have received and the camaraderie of this group. When I submitted I was not really sure what to write in the details section but as I look at other ribbon winning photos I see where comments can be helpful. <br/> <br/>Photo and the meaning:<br/> <br/>The shot was taken mid afternoon on a cloudy day in Chandler Arizona about a mile deep into the desert. My 11yr old daughter was the model wearing one of my wifes nightgowns. The point of the picture is that children have a gift of not seeing the big picture and the day to day tribulations of life which is seen much clearer as we become adults (crime, poverty, etc.). The empty drawers symbolize minimal possessions, the dying tree represents aging and sitting alone in the middle of the desert represents an emotion of no purpose. But not all is lost as the child has the gift to block out this negativity and conjure a feeling of peace and contentment with taking in the moment and splendor of the beautiful sky. If only everyone in world had this gift, imagine <br/> <br/>How it was done:<br/> <br/>Basically I went to a local hardware store and purchased a piece of door trim (about 5 feet long), mounted it to the frame and drove the door trim into the ground with a hammer. I used sticks and other items to prop up the stacked drawers. <br/> <br/>Again thanks for all the votes and feedback. <br/> <br/>HB   <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the votes and constructive candid feedback and of course the ribbon. What a confidence builder. As a newbe I am impressed with the welcome I have received and the camaraderie of this group. When I submitted I was not really sure what to write in the details section but as I look at other ribbon winning photos I see where comments can be helpful.  Photo and the meaning: The shot was taken mid afternoon on a cloudy day in Chandler Arizona about a mile deep into the desert. My 11yr old daughter was the model wearing one of my wifes nightgowns. The point of the picture is that children have a gift of not seeing the big picture and the day to day tribulations of life which is seen much clearer as we become adults (crime, poverty, etc.). The empty drawers symbolize minimal possessions, the dying tree represents aging and sitting alone in the middle of the desert represents an emotion of no purpose. But not all is lost as the child has the gift to block out this negativity and conjure a feeling of peace and contentment with taking in the moment and splendor of the beautiful sky. If only everyone in world had this gift, imagine  How it was done: Basically I went to a local hardware store and purchased a piece of door trim (about 5 feet long), mounted it to the frame and drove the door trim into the ground with a hammer. I used sticks and other items to prop up the stacked drawers.  Again thanks for all the votes and feedback.  HB      ', '2005-03-17 02:48:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1234044, 153371, 18219, '<td valign="top">Wow, a very deep meaning behind it.<br/>Did you set out with that meaning in mind or make the meaning fit the finished product?<br/>Regardless, a great picture.<br/></td>', 'Wow, a very deep meaning behind it.Did you set out with that meaning in mind or make the meaning fit the finished product?Regardless, a great picture.', '2005-03-17 07:34:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1234104, 154154, 5515, '<td valign="top">Just an FYI. If your friend fired the shutter, he actually owns the rights to the image since he actually ''took'' the picture. I am sure it will fly by here on DPC but in the real world it''s copyright infringement.<br/> <br/>Great image none the less...</td>', 'Just an FYI. If your friend fired the shutter, he actually owns the rights to the image since he actually ''took'' the picture. I am sure it will fly by here on DPC but in the real world it''s copyright infringement. Great image none the less...', '2005-03-17 08:20:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1234134, 154154, 17613, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Davenit:</b></div><hr/><i> Just an FYI. If your friend fired the shutter, he actually owns the rights to the image since he actually ''took'' the picture. I am sure it will fly by here on DPC but in the real world it''s copyright infringement.<br/> <br/>Great image none the less... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No copyright or rules infringement here unless the last part of the rule was not obtained, or the administrators object:<br/> <br/><b>Ownership:</b>The photograph you enter must be taken and post-processed by you. You may let someone else press the shutter if you are unable to, but you must be the one who set up the shot and configured the camera. If you wish to collaborate with others when creating your submission, you will need express permission from the administrators beforehand. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Davenit: Just an FYI. If your friend fired the shutter, he actually owns the rights to the image since he actually ''took'' the picture. I am sure it will fly by here on DPC but in the real world it''s copyright infringement. Great image none the less...   No copyright or rules infringement here unless the last part of the rule was not obtained, or the administrators object: Ownership:The photograph you enter must be taken and post-processed by you. You may let someone else press the shutter if you are unable to, but you must be the one who set up the shot and configured the camera. If you wish to collaborate with others when creating your submission, you will need express permission from the administrators beforehand. ', '2005-03-17 08:51:48.000000', NULL, 0),
