(1243618, 154133, 15711, '<td valign="top">Rules? Schmules! Let''s not get picky about the semantics of rules or the "ethics" of the contest. Everything is up to interpretation and I think the photo is a true wonder.  This is a venue to learn and be creative, so I say HURRAY for your effort.  Wish I had the patience to go to that much trouble.<br/> <br/>Way to go!!!!</td>', 'Rules? Schmules! Let''s not get picky about the semantics of rules or the "ethics" of the contest. Everything is up to interpretation and I think the photo is a true wonder.  This is a venue to learn and be creative, so I say HURRAY for your effort.  Wish I had the patience to go to that much trouble. Way to go!!!!', '2005-03-22 18:50:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1244226, 153545, 34217, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>     Your concept for this photo is unclear to me and is there for hard for me to place it in the surreal challenge.  But also remeber that I can''t read your mind so it could very well be surreal to you.  I will only critique from a photographic stand point and not about your concept.  I think that your lighting could be improved, maybe a stronger side light and more shadow.  I prefer more dramatic light 80% of the time.  I like that it is not centered from top to bottom, but the pawns feel a little tight at the top.  I don''t mind the softness of the shot, from noise reduction  I am assuming.  I think you should even play around with making a little softer, maybe add some noise???  Also the tones are so beautiful I would have liked to see it without.  Please remember that these are all suggestions and the best way to figure out what you like best is to make changes and compare, sometimes it just helps to have another set of eyes to help with changes.  In the end you need to make your photo what you want it to be and if you love it, don''t worry about what anyone else has to say.  Overall it is intersting, but please let me know what your concept was I am very interested.</td>', 'Critique Club     Your concept for this photo is unclear to me and is there for hard for me to place it in the surreal challenge.  But also remeber that I can''t read your mind so it could very well be surreal to you.  I will only critique from a photographic stand point and not about your concept.  I think that your lighting could be improved, maybe a stronger side light and more shadow.  I prefer more dramatic light 80% of the time.  I like that it is not centered from top to bottom, but the pawns feel a little tight at the top.  I don''t mind the softness of the shot, from noise reduction  I am assuming.  I think you should even play around with making a little softer, maybe add some noise???  Also the tones are so beautiful I would have liked to see it without.  Please remember that these are all suggestions and the best way to figure out what you like best is to make changes and compare, sometimes it just helps to have another set of eyes to help with changes.  In the end you need to make your photo what you want it to be and if you love it, don''t worry about what anyone else has to say.  Overall it is intersting, but please let me know what your concept was I am very interested.', '2005-03-22 23:40:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1244511, 154133, 18065, '<td valign="top">very very very nice!!!</td>', 'very very very nice!!!', '2005-03-23 00:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1246227, 153324, 31606, '<td valign="top">I would like to see more sky in this and maybe bring that highest peak to the left more.  I see you entered this in the surreal challenge.  If you would have entered this into the AA Challenge or a challenge more fitting then I think you would have done a lot better.  Although an average vote of 4.870 is still good at this website.  You have an eye for this stuff.</td>', 'I would like to see more sky in this and maybe bring that highest peak to the left more.  I see you entered this in the surreal challenge.  If you would have entered this into the AA Challenge or a challenge more fitting then I think you would have done a lot better.  Although an average vote of 4.870 is still good at this website.  You have an eye for this stuff.', '2005-03-23 17:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1247095, 153324, 1827, '<td valign="top">Coming from the "Want Comments?" thread.  You''re probably fed up with "doesn''t meet the challenge" type comments, especially since the challenge is over, but I''m curious what your take on this was in terms of surrealism.  It is a lovely photo, and I like the interplay of shadow and light.  You exposed the sky and the snow perfectly, which isn''t an easy task, so A+ there.</td>', 'Coming from the "Want Comments?" thread.  You''re probably fed up with "doesn''t meet the challenge" type comments, especially since the challenge is over, but I''m curious what your take on this was in terms of surrealism.  It is a lovely photo, and I like the interplay of shadow and light.  You exposed the sky and the snow perfectly, which isn''t an easy task, so A+ there.', '2005-03-23 22:51:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1247185, 153324, 27164, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by just-married:</b></div><hr/><i> Coming from the "Want Comments?" thread.  You''re probably fed up with "doesn''t meet the challenge" type comments, especially since the challenge is over, but I''m curious what your take on this was in terms of surrealism.  It is a lovely photo, and I like the interplay of shadow and light.  You exposed the sky and the snow perfectly, which isn''t an easy task, so A+ there. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess I didn''t fully understand the meaning of surrealism - I thought that a landscape, if done properly, could be surreal - I thought I had the best image I could for the challenge anyway<br/> <br/>Justin</td>', 'Originally posted by just-married: Coming from the "Want Comments?" thread.  You''re probably fed up with "doesn''t meet the challenge" type comments, especially since the challenge is over, but I''m curious what your take on this was in terms of surrealism.  It is a lovely photo, and I like the interplay of shadow and light.  You exposed the sky and the snow perfectly, which isn''t an easy task, so A+ there.   I guess I didn''t fully understand the meaning of surrealism - I thought that a landscape, if done properly, could be surreal - I thought I had the best image I could for the challenge anyway Justin', '2005-03-24 00:01:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1247609, 154135, 35122, '<td valign="top">Very Nice...I want to be there...exploring!!!  Great job!!</td>', 'Very Nice...I want to be there...exploring!!!  Great job!!', '2005-03-24 10:28:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1248394, 153545, 20056, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comment Jmoore!<br/>As a chess player, one of my erotic dreams have been playing chess over a woman nude body...<br/>Dali also used chess symbols like horses and elephants with catholic simbols (crosses) in his paintings together with nude women <a href="//www.galeria.sonic.pl/DaliGal/Gal20/1946_01.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.galeria.sonic.pl/DaliGal/Gal20/1946_01.htm</a> <br/>In my favor, I could say that the model was pretty sensitive (You can notice the movement of the standed pieces) and I did not have much time for the picture :)<br/>I wanted to give a fogy aspect like a dream... but many people got lost in the fog, and as I said before: the blue tone doesnot fit in my book very much :(.  You are right: the light could be improved (maybe with another camera :).<br/>Thanks again.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jmoore:</b></div><hr/><i> Critique Club<br/>     Your concept for this photo is unclear to me and is there for hard for me to place it in the surreal challenge.  But also remeber that I can''t read your mind so it could very well be surreal to you.  I will only critique from a photographic stand point and not about your concept.  I think that your lighting could be improved, maybe a stronger side light and more shadow.  I prefer more dramatic light 80% of the time.  I like that it is not centered from top to bottom, but the pawns feel a little tight at the top.  I don''t mind the softness of the shot, from noise reduction  I am assuming.  I think you should even play around with making a little softer, maybe add some noise???  Also the tones are so beautiful I would have liked to see it without.  Please remember that these are all suggestions and the best way to figure out what you like best is to make changes and compare, sometimes it just helps to have another set of eyes to help with changes.  In the end you need to make your photo what you want it to be and if you love it, don''t worry about what anyone else has to say.  Overall it is intersting, but please let me know what your concept was I am very interested. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-25 16:39:10.</i></td>', 'Thanks for your comment Jmoore!As a chess player, one of my erotic dreams have been playing chess over a woman nude body...Dali also used chess symbols like horses and elephants with catholic simbols (crosses) in his paintings together with nude women //www.galeria.sonic.pl/DaliGal/Gal20/1946_01.htm In my favor, I could say that the model was pretty sensitive (You can notice the movement of the standed pieces) and I did not have much time for the picture :)I wanted to give a fogy aspect like a dream... but many people got lost in the fog, and as I said before: the blue tone doesnot fit in my book very much :(.  You are right: the light could be improved (maybe with another camera :).Thanks again. Originally posted by jmoore: Critique Club     Your concept for this photo is unclear to me and is there for hard for me to place it in the surreal challenge.  But also remeber that I can''t read your mind so it could very well be surreal to you.  I will only critique from a photographic stand point and not about your concept.  I think that your lighting could be improved, maybe a stronger side light and more shadow.  I prefer more dramatic light 80% of the time.  I like that it is not centered from top to bottom, but the pawns feel a little tight at the top.  I don''t mind the softness of the shot, from noise reduction  I am assuming.  I think you should even play around with making a little softer, maybe add some noise???  Also the tones are so beautiful I would have liked to see it without.  Please remember that these are all suggestions and the best way to figure out what you like best is to make changes and compare, sometimes it just helps to have another set of eyes to help with changes.  In the end you need to make your photo what you want it to be and if you love it, don''t worry about what anyone else has to say.  Overall it is intersting, but please let me know what your concept was I am very interested. ', '2005-03-24 19:31:55.000000', '2005-03-25 16:39:10.000000', 0),
(1249188, 153324, 5792, '<td valign="top">The image shows a bit of the jaggies along some edges. The clouds on the left lack detail and are overexposed. Overall it is a nice scene and good picture. I suspect the lower score is not so much because of the picture itself, but because it was not "surreal" enough for the challenge to some voters. I scored it 6.</td>', 'The image shows a bit of the jaggies along some edges. The clouds on the left lack detail and are overexposed. Overall it is a nice scene and good picture. I suspect the lower score is not so much because of the picture itself, but because it was not "surreal" enough for the challenge to some voters. I scored it 6.', '2005-03-25 07:49:58.000000', NULL, 0),
